{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.diag_conj_necessary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.diag_conj_necessary","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L100-L121","doc":"Diagonal conjugation in a 2-dim representation preserves the diagonal and the product of\nthe off-diagonal entries. (In the irrep `(2,1)` of `H_3` with `σ_a` diagonal, the elements\ncommuting with the interface letter act diagonally, so these are necessary conditions for a\nnucleon to be mirror-fixed up to that centraliser.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.interface_rescues_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.interface_rescues_iff","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L86-L92","doc":"Over a domain, an interface in the subalgebra generated by `s` gives `pn = np` iff it is\ntrivial (`b = 0`) or the bare-letter bonds already agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.interface_bond_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.interface_bond_difference","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L76-L84","doc":"With equal free terms, the bond difference for the interface `a + b • s` is `b` times the\nbare-letter bond difference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.placement_exchange_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.placement_exchange_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L56-L68","doc":"**Reflected placement is exchange-covariant.** Let `eL eR : B → A` be the two block\nembeddings, commuting with each other, and let the half twist `F` send the left block to the\nright block (and back) through the in-block mirror `m`, an involution. Put the *mirrored*\nnucleon on the right: `X x y = eL x * eR (m y)`. Then `F (X x y) = X y x`, so the bonds agree\nfor every pair of nucleon words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.exchange_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.exchange_forced","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L49-L54","doc":"If a `Φ`-preserving automorphism fixing `s` maps the `pn` word to the `np` word, the two\nbonds agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.bond_transport_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.bond_transport_anti","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L43-L47","doc":"A `Φ`-preserving anti-automorphism fixing `s`, with `Φ` cyclic, transports the bond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.bond_transport_aut","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.bond_transport_aut","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeltaLambdaMirrorTransport.lean#L38-L41","doc":"A `Φ`-preserving ring automorphism fixing the interface letter transports the bond. ","signatureChunk":0}]}